  "text": "Suibhne was a king of a small region of Ulster. He went to war to help the king of the province, but a curse hung over him. He had treated a monk, Saint Rónán, with contempt, so the saint cursed him. When the fighting began, Suibhne lost his wits and fled his post. He thought he was a bird, so he hid in a yew tree. He moved from tree to tree as his people searched for him. At last he came to a monastery, thought to be at Rosharkin in County Antrim or at a glen in County Kerry. A relative, dressed as an old woman, earned his trust and brought him home. Then the woman showed him how high he used to leap. He tried it again and lost his senses. He wandered to a monastery in County Carlow and spoke with Saint Molling. As he told his story, a jealous husband killed him with a spear. Suibhne is not on any king list, so scholars read him as a form of the wild seer Merlin.",
